  "instructions": [
    "Heat the coconut oil in a large pan over medium heat and cook the onion for 8-10 minutes until softened.",
    "Add the garlic, ginger and fresh red chili and continue to cook for another minute until fragrant.",
    "Stir in the ground coriander, ground cumin, turmeric and cayenne pepper and cook for a further minute, stirring occasionally.",
    "Add the tomato paste and stir well to combine, then add the chicken cubes. Toss well to combine with the spices and cook for 3-4 minutes until the chicken is sealed.",
    "Next, add the cubed potatoes, diced tomatoes, chicken stock and salt. Stir well to combine, then bring to a simmer. Cover the pan and cook for 10 minutes or until the potatoes are fork-tender.",
    "Stir in the coconut milk and continue to simmer for another minute until heated through. Adjust the seasoning to taste, add the fresh cilantro and serve."
